Dear Procurement Operations and Deal Team Leads,

As we kick off the Q3 2026 supplier contract onboarding cycle, it is critical that we align our automated systems and manual reviews with our updated governance model.

For pipeline volume, procurement should work from normal in-flight POs only. Records marked `Exception` are not part of the cumulative volume calculation; the active normal statuses are `Booked`, `In Transit`, and `At Port`.

For Jira, active deal tasks should land in `In Review` in the `PROJ` project. The workflow map in the procurement pipeline workbook documents the allowed path into that state and the direct transitions that are blocked by governance.

For owner and sizing, use the Q3 pipeline workbook as the source: `SupplierMaster.primary_owner_id` maps to `ProcurementOwners.employee_id`, and the active Deal Size thresholds are the Large, Medium, and Standard rows in `DealSizeBuckets`. Legacy micro or macro sizes should not be used for this onboarding cycle.

This onboarding cycle is essential to secure our tier-1 and tier-2 material supplies for the upcoming fiscal quarters. Let us ensure the transition data is 100% accurate before the active board review.

